{"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Building","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Contributing","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AdaUIIdentity","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ImageDecoders","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationAuthoring","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/CharacterLocomotion3D","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationIK","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Atmosphere","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/GameDiagnosticsOverlay","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/MovieMaker","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/PipelinedRendering","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/DLSSUpscaling","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/HardwarePathTracing","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Terrain","doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/VisionOSWindowed"],"generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ProceduralNoise","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Use a noise generator as a deterministic scalar field for terrain heights,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"procedural placement, or volume density. Import ","type":"text"},{"code":"Math","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" directly, or use its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"re-export from ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdaEngine","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". No GPU or editor state is needed.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Sample seeded Perlin noise","anchor":"Sample-seeded-Perlin-noise","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PerlinNoise2D"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PerlinNoise3D"},{"type":"text","text":" return values within "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-1...1"},{"type":"text","text":" for finite"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"coordinates and frequency. Fixed seeds and coordinates produce repeatable samples;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sampling does not advance a random generator. These are hashed-gradient Perlin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"variants with quintic interpolation, not bit-compatible implementations of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"canonical permutation-table algorithm. 2D noise is its own field, not a 3D slice."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Math","","let perlin = PerlinNoise2D(seed: 1234)","let heightVariation = perlin.sample(at: Vector2(12.5, 8.25))","let volume = PerlinNoise3D(seed: 1234)","let density = volume.sample(at: Vector3(12.5, 8.25, -2))"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Layer-terrain-detail-with-FBM","text":"Layer terrain detail with FBM","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FractalNoise"},{"type":"text","text":" combines samples at increasing frequencies and decreasing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"amplitudes. This example computes a height; it does not modify a terrain entity."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let terrain = FractalNoise(","    source: PerlinNoise2D(seed: 1234),","    octaves: 5,","    frequency: 0.02,","    lacunarity: 2,","    persistence: 0.5",")","let worldX: Float = 32","let worldZ: Float = -16","let height = terrain.sample(at: Vector2(worldX, worldZ)) * 20"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"octaves","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": number of layers, clamped to ","type":"text"},{"code":"1...32","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"frequency","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": base coordinate scale. Nonfinite\/non-positive settings become ","type":"text"},{"code":"1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lacunarity"},{"type":"text","text":": frequency multiplier between octaves. Nonfinite\/non-positive settings become "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"persistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": amplitude multiplier between octaves, clamped to ","type":"text"},{"code":"0...1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Nonfinite settings become ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.5","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Zero uses only the first octave.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Output is divided by the sum of active octave amplitudes. Sources bounded to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-1...1"},{"type":"text","text":" stay within that range; custom source ranges are not clipped."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The optional "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sample(at:frequency:)"},{"type":"text","text":" argument multiplies the base frequency,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"including when fractal fields are nested. Zero or negative call frequencies are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"valid coordinate transforms; the initializer’s positive settings have the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"normalization rules above."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Implement-a-custom-generator","text":"Implement a custom generator","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Noise"},{"type":"text","text":" has an associated "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Point"},{"type":"text","text":" type inferred from the sampling method. A 2D"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"implementation cannot accidentally be called with a 3D point. A custom field only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"needs to be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"text":" and implement one method:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["struct RidgeNoise: Noise {","    func sample(at point: Vector2, frequency: Double) -> Double {","        let x = Double(point.x) * frequency","        return 1 - abs(Math.sin(x))","    }","}","","let ridges = FractalNoise(source: RidgeNoise(), frequency: 0.1)","let ridgeHeight = ridges.sample(at: Vector2(10, 20))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the same type for a custom terrain field that composes several generators."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"An immutable struct is usually sufficient; no base class or shared mutable seed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is necessary. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Noise.sample(at:)"},{"type":"text","text":" also works in generic code, using unit frequency."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Limits-and-invalid-input","text":"Limits and invalid input","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vector2\/Vector3 store Float coordinates. Double interpolation cannot recover","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"precision already lost in a large world position; use local coordinates before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conversion for fine detail far from the origin. No serialization, shader noise,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"terrain wiring, or cross-library sample compatibility is provided here.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Perlin sampling returns NaN for nonfinite inputs or coordinate-scaling overflow."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"FBM returns NaN for nonfinite call frequency or active-octave frequency overflow,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and propagates invalid samples from its source. Custom sources define their own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"coordinate validation. Check "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isFinite"},{"type":"text","text":" before storing a computed terrain height;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"invalid sample input is not silently converted to a valid height."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Terrain","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the separate terrain creation and editing API."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/adaengine\/proceduralnoise"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"AdaEngine"}],"role":"article","title":"Procedural Noise"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine"]]},"references":{"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/AnimationAuthoring":{"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/animationauthoring","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Copy an imported animation or capture a rest\/current pose into a project-owned"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".animlib"},{"type":"text","text":" resource. Source GLB\/glTF bytes remain unchanged. Swift code, Studio’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Animator, the editor agent and project Tools share the same data and edit commands.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Authoring skeletal animation","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationAuthoring"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/GameDiagnosticsOverlay":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See the game’s update rate while you play. The overlay shows "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"FPS"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Frame time"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in the top-left corner of the game window. Mouse and keyboard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"input still reach the game under the overlay.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/GameDiagnosticsOverlay","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Game diagnostics overlay","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/gamediagnosticsoverlay"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Building":{"abstract":[{"text":"This guide covers two scenarios:","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Building","role":"article","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Building Ada","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/building"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/HardwarePathTracing":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Let a path-traced view find ray intersections with the GPU’s ray-tracing hardware instead of a shader BVH. The image,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lighting and denoisers stay the same; only the intersection step changes, and the shader BVH remains the fallback"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wherever hardware cannot be used.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/hardwarepathtracing","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Hardware Path Tracing","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/HardwarePathTracing"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/AdaUIIdentity":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AdaUIIdentity","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/adauiidentity","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"AdaUI reconciles a new view tree against the mounted "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ViewNode"},{"text":" tree. A node is preserved only when the new node and old node describe the same identity and the new node can update the old node. Preserved nodes keep their ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", focus state, in-flight animation controllers, layers, and other node-local runtime state. Recreated nodes start with fresh runtime state."}],"type":"topic","title":"AdaUI View Identity"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/VisionOSWindowed":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/VisionOSWindowed","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/visionoswindowed","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"visionOS Windowed Mode","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Run Ada apps in visionOS Shared Space using the existing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WindowGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" scene model."}]},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/MovieMaker":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/MovieMaker","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a fresh game world at a fixed simulation rate, waiting for every GPU"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame and disk write before advancing. Rendering speed never drops movie frames."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Configure the same gameplay plugins and cameras as your game in "},{"code":"make","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Platform\/window plugins are unnecessary for this offscreen runtime."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"MovieMaker","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MovieMaker"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/moviemaker","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MovieMaker"}]},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/CharacterLocomotion3D":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/CharacterLocomotion3D","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/characterlocomotion3d","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CharacterLocomotion3DComponent"},{"type":"text","text":" to play skeletal animations from an upright 3D character’s"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"actual movement. Add it to the root entity that owns the character controller and skinned model."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Your input or AI continues to set "},{"code":"desiredVelocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jumpRequested"},{"type":"text","text":". Locomotion reads the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"resolved motion after physics, so holding forward against a wall can leave the character idle.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Animate a 3D character from movement"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Atmosphere":{"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/atmosphere","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Give a 3D camera a physically based sky. The atmosphere scatters the sun’s light"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the way air does, so the sky turns from blue at noon to orange near the horizon","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and dark at night, the sun appears as a disc that the air reddens, and distant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"geometry fades into haze."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Atmosphere","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Atmosphere"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Terrain":{"url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/terrain","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create editable ground with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Terrain3D"},{"type":"text","text":". Its heights describe one square surface"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the entity’s local X\/Z plane. "},{"code":"Model3DPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" generates the visible geometry;","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Physics3DPlugin"},{"text":" adds matching static triangle collision.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","type":"topic","title":"Terrain","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Terrain"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/AnimationIK":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Constrain a skeletal chain after its clip, Animation Graph and visual LOD pose have been mixed."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/animationik","type":"topic","title":"Animation IK and pose modifiers","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/AnimationIK"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/Contributing":{"abstract":[{"text":"We welcome contributions of all kinds: bug fixes, features, documentation, and examples.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/Contributing","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Contributing to Ada","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/contributing"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/DLSSUpscaling":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/DLSSUpscaling","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/dlssupscaling","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Render a 3D view below its output resolution and reconstruct it with NVIDIA DLSS Super Resolution, or denoise a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path-traced view with DLSS Ray Reconstruction. DLSS is optional: without it a camera uses the portable temporal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"reconstruction that ships with the engine, and nothing else changes."}],"type":"topic","title":"DLSS Upscaling"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/ImageDecoders":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/ImageDecoders","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/imagedecoders","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Load PNG, JPEG (","type":"text"},{"code":"jpg","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"jpeg","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), BMP and TGA images as CPU pixels using","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Image","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or load a GPU texture through ","type":"text"},{"code":"Texture2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"Loading images and adding formats"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine/PipelinedRendering":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine\/PipelinedRendering","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine\/pipelinedrendering","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Render a scene one frame behind its simulation to overlap rendering with the next frame’s work."}],"type":"topic","title":"Pipelined Rendering"},"doc://AdaEngine/documentation/AdaEngine":{"abstract":[{"text":"Bringing simple and powerful game engine for your awesome games.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AdaEngine\/documentation\/AdaEngine","role":"collection","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/adaengine","kind":"symbol","title":"AdaEngine"}}}